<title>USA: Neb. power doubles short-term debt cap to $150 mln.</title>
<headline>Neb. power doubles short-term debt cap to $150 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nebraska Public Power District on Friday approved doubling its authorization on tax-exempt commercial paper from $75 million to $150 million, Assistant Treasurer Traci Bender said.</p>
<p>The district currently has $52 million of tax-exempt commercial paper outstanding and plans to sell about $10 million of short-term debt in the next few months, Bender added.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, Chicago Newsroom, 312-408-8647))</p>
